I recently played a wizard, and got much farther than I ever had
before.  I think much of this is due to the special property of

<spoiler>



























athames (they never go dull)--thus allowing me to engrave the magic
word "Elbereth" (the only monsters I have found that this doesn't work
against are @'s and minotaurs.  Am I missing any?).  Although
engravings will eventually wear off if you fight from them, you can
always reengrave them (and checking your engraving takes no time at
all, so you can do this without ever getting hit).

Now, as you may know, most valuable gems are "hard"--that is, they
canbe used to engrave, just like a weapon.  My question:  are they as
hard as athames?  That is, do they never go dull?

If this is true, as just about any class has access to some hard gems
not too deep in the Gnomish mines, this is a _powerful_ spoiler.
Forget about mumakil deaths once and for all.  Same goes for Vampire
Lords, and even demons.  If you couple it with a
shield of reflection (always my first wish nowadays, after one too
many encounters with the business end of wands of death), dragons are
no threat either.

